# Restraint Bias

The tendency to overestimate our ability to control impulses. People who believe they have strong self-control often fail to prepare for situations where impulses will be strong.

## Key Points
- Overconfidence in self-control leads to poor preparation
- Connects to [[overconfidence-and-certainty]] — overestimating abilities
- Planning fallacy of self-control — underestimating when temptation will strike

## Guardrail
Rather than assuming you can resist temptation, design environments that reduce temptation exposure. Use [[time-delay-decisions]] for emotional choices.
